Two more things needed:
- handle `Data` lifetime, by using a raw pointer. This would allow it to survive the current function like `qemu_plugin_install`.
- Declare our callback data as Sync, so we can call this concurrently. Requires a mutex on top of our Data.
  It's also possible to play with atomics, or mutex per field.

```rust
// One generic wrapper per callback register. It ensures we have a matching between callbacktype
// and userdata.
fn register_callback<T: Sync>(cb: fn(TranslationBlock, &T), userdata: &T) {
    unsafe {
        register_callback_c(
            std::mem::transmute(cb),
            userdata as *const T as *mut c_void,
        )
    }
}

pub struct Data {
    str: String,
}

fn main() {
    let msg_ptr = Box::into_raw(Box::new(Mutex::new(Data {
        str: String::from("Hello World"),
    })));
    let msg: &Mutex<Data> = unsafe { &*msg_ptr };

    register_callback(
        |tb: TranslationBlock, s: &Mutex<Data>| {
            let mut data = s.lock().unwrap();
            data.str.push_str("!");
            println!("{} (addr={:#x}, length={})", data.str, tb.addr(), tb.length());
        },
        msg,
    );
    println!("after: {}", msg.lock().unwrap().str);

    // at exit, free our data
    drop(unsafe { Box::from_raw(msg_ptr) });
}
```

